  "articleBody": "When you’re thinking about new tile for your bathroom, it’s not just about what looks good – it’s about what works best for each area! Different parts of your bathroom have different needs, so picking the right material is key. For floors, you want something durable and slip-resistant. Porcelain is a fantastic choice here because it's super tough, resistant to water, and comes in tons of styles. Ceramic is also a good option, often more budget-friendly. Natural stone like marble or travertine looks luxurious but requires more maintenance, including regular sealing, and can be slippery when wet, so you’ll want to consider that for flooring. For shower walls, water absorption is a big factor. Again, porcelain and ceramic shine here because they’re nearly impervious to water. Natural stone can be used, but it absolutely needs proper sealing and ongoing maintenance to prevent water damage and staining. Backer board and waterproofing membranes are critical regardless of your tile choice in wet areas. For accent walls or areas outside the direct splash zone, you have more flexibility. You could go for decorative ceramic tiles, glass mosaics, or even some types of engineered stone panels. Understanding these differences helps you make smart choices that'll last. We can walk you through the pros and cons of each material for your specific project; just ask!",
